- **The 2025 U&L amendment's lounge-tier obligation is not public.** Card 3 makes the American position on this the leading indicator; the entire shell allowance is contingent on the answer. If the answer is "no obligation," the shell is a real-options decision that requires a signed AA cost-recovery memorandum above the $10M threshold set here.
- **Detroit McNamara sourcing remains trade-press.** I did not re-open primary sourcing this round. The historical case is now buttressed by LGA Terminal C and Heathrow T5 as analogues, so the affirmative side no longer stands on one weakly-sourced case (per C-19).
