## Implications for the operator

Six decisions, ordered by quarter. The board digests one to three decisions per quarter; presenting six as first-move equivalents is how the board approves none of them.

**Q1 (next board cycle):** Adopt the register as a Board policy resolution (Card 1). Open the U&L side-letter conversation on the four Category A options as a package (Cards 2, 3, 4, 5). Obtain the release-for-fabrication schedule from Innovation Next+ within 15 days of adoption and populate the register table (see below). These three actions are a coherent first quarter.

**Q2:** Commission the 2043 international peak-hour forecast (Card 4 first operational deliverable) as a self-funded procurement — $250–500K, 6–9 months, standard consultant panel (Ricondo, LeighFisher, Landrum & Brown). Confirm current Phase 1 Skylink node design intent from Innovation Next+ within 30 days (Card 5 first move). Confirm mezzanine-vs-at-grade siting assumption for the Flagship shell with the fabricator (Card 3 first move).

**Q3:** Fund the operational-readiness discipline the historical record has been naming since ACRP Synthesis 20 — seat operations at module-level factory design reviews with veto authority, witness testing at the factory, contract each module seam as a mapped "operator interface plane" so MEP, low-voltage, and BHS branches can be re-terminated in 2038 without breaching structure.[^50] Deliverable: a written specification before the next module design lock, deposited in DFW's CMMS at commissioning. Adopt the Terminal F O&M reserve policy (see below).

**Terminal F O&M reserve policy** (F-7 rewrite). Not "fund the second bill" — a specific ask. Establish a Terminal F O&M reserve, sized to 1.5% of depreciated asset value annually, adopted concurrent with facility acceptance, treated as an above-the-line rate-base charge under the U&L. Baseline components: BHS 15-year cycle at ~10% of purchase cost/year in EDS maintenance; HVAC and BMS 15–20 years; apron pavement first meaningful rehab in the 10–15 year window under AC 150/5380-7B; PBBs 20–25 years with mid-life overhauls.[^51] Underfunding by 15% generates a nine-figure deferred-maintenance liability inside 20 years.

**Publishing the register externally is cut.** Publishing option prices for a live capital program tips DFW's hand in every future rate conversation with American, creates a downgrade trigger the airport did not need to create, and does not clear its costs against a rating differential the evidence base cannot measure. The register is an internal-audit and board-materials instrument. Selective disclosure in a specific rating cycle when the analytical case supports it is a separate future decision, not a Q1 action.

